{
  "provenance": {
    "source": "hand-authored",
    "date": "2026-09-19",
    "evidence": "changes/2026-09-19-cloud-identity-and-endpoints.md (D1 named credentials, D2 provenance, D4 endpoint override); spec/auth.md AUTH-1 named credentials, AUTH-7 named mode and base URL, AUTH-10 endpoint (amended 2026-09-19). Rung kinds are the ones auth/resolution.json already pins; a named case lists only the rungs the name covers, in chain order, because a named credential never falls through."
  },
  "description": "AUTH-1 named credentials through the AUTH-7 doctor, offline. Each case names one identity (`credential`) for a cloud door; `expect.steps` are exactly the rungs the doctor walks (rung 0 `api_keys` then the name's rungs) with their states; `expect.base_url` is the URL the door will send to when `base_url` (an explicit endpoint root) or a vendor endpoint variable is present; `expect.error` (a regex over the message) marks a configuration the implementation must refuse before any walk. Files are materialized under a sandbox HOME by the harness; `~/` means that HOME. The sentinel must never appear in any rendered surface.",
  "sentinel": "SECRET-SENTINEL-DO-NOT-PRINT",
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "azure-platform-managed-identity-unprobed",
      "provider": "azure",
      "credential": "platform",
      "env": {
        "AZURE_OPENAI_RESOURCE": "acme",
        "IDENTITY_ENDPOINT": "http://127.0.0.1:41/msi/token",
        "IDENTITY_HEADER": "SECRET-SENTINEL-DO-NOT-PRINT",
        "PATH": "~/bin"
      },
      "files": {
        "~/bin/az": "#!/bin/sh\nexit 1\n"
      },
      "expect": {
        "configured": true,
        "steps": [
          {
            "kind": "api_keys",
            "state": "absent"
          },
          {
            "kind": "managed-identity",
            "state": "unprobed"
          }
        ],
        "base_url": "https://acme.openai.azure.com/openai/v1"
      }
    },
